s dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas. Strengths: situational awareness, technical cognition, leadership. Weaknesses: attitude (show-off, not open) could affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Weaknesses: hot temper, know-it-all attitude (cooperation).\n\nWe need to start discussion. Choose a candidate? Perhaps Candidate C seems strong technically and leadership, but attitude concerns. Candidate B has reliability but interpersonal issues. Candidate A has decision speed but communication issues. Candidate D has problem solving but hot temper.\n\nWhich is best overall? Might be Candidate C: strong situational awareness, leadership, technical, but need to address attitude. Could argue that technical competence outweighs attitude concerns, but need to discuss.\n\nAlternatively, Candidate B's conscientiousness and stress handling are key, but nasty remarks are serious for crew cooperation.\n\nI think start by highlighting Candidate C's strengths and concerns, and propose as leading candidate but note concerns. Provide vote.\n\nLet's produce public message: vote for Candidate C, explain strengths (anticipates danger, sees complex connections, leadership) and concerns (show-off, not open). Suggest need to probe attitude further but still best fit.\n\nProceed."}
